Translation patch: <Pippenger as VartimeMultiscalarMul>::optional_multiscalar_mul

Change: scalars are collected first and `size = scalars.len()` replaces `size_hint().0`; the
scalar/point `zip` becomes a helper with an explicit `next` loop; the lazy column iterator + `fold` becomes a reversed
range loop accumulating `total` (highest column first, as `fold` did).
Why: Aeneas only models `Iterator::next` (aeneas#1057).
Behaviour: same result, not identical: the window width uses the exact length (equal for exact-size
inputs; any width gives the same result); scalars are read before points; an unbounded scalar
iterator with finite points no longer terminates (with edwards-optional_multiscalar_mul.patch
applied, the caller collects both inputs and checks their actual lengths first).

